Here is a Java program that takes a number as input and prints the factorial of that number using recursion:

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class FactorialCalculator {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Enter a number: ");

        try {
            int number = scanner.nextInt();
            if (number < 0) {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid input. The number must be a non-negative integer.");
            }

            System.out.println("Calculating factorial of " + number + "...");
            int factorial = calculateFactorial(number);
            System.out.println("The factorial of " + number + " is " + factorial);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            System.out.println("Error: " + e.getMessage());
        } finally {
            scanner.close();
        }
    }

    public static int calculateFactorial(int number) {
        if (number == 0 || number == 1) {
            return 1;
        }

        System.out.println("Calculating factorial of " + (number - 1) + "...");
        int factorial = calculateFactorial(number - 1);
        return number * factorial;
    }
}
```

